#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Guarded host-side Arch rootfs installer for the Samsung SM-X810.

This intentionally mirrors Fedora's guided install safety model while keeping
the Arch trial narrower: TWRP must already be open, and the sole block-device
write is formatting the existing PARTLABEL=linuxroot as ext4. Before formatting,
it saves the Android boot set to the host and seeds it into the new rootfs. It
never writes GPT, Android userdata, boot images, recovery, vbmeta, or reboots.
"""

